  "id": "2e9c9de4-2e51-4c11-aadf-caf380bc3981",
  "message": "I checked with toyota_mechanic: Diagnosis only — nothing was changed.\n\n**Why the pause happens:** Toyota's speech queue plays sentences one at a time, strictly in sequence. For each sentence, it waits for that sentence's audio to fully finish playing *before* it even starts asking the text-to-speech service to generate the next one. That generation step (a network call to Edge TTS) takes a moment — and during that moment, there's silence. So every period/sentence boundary includes a dead gap while the next sentence is still being synthesized.\n\nThis is a known, already-documented gap in the code (the spec notes \"no overlap\" between sentences), not something newly discovered.\n\n**What would fix it (not done, per diagnose-only):** start generating sentence N+1's audio while sentence N is still playing, instead of waiting until N finishes. Toyota already has this exact \"one-ahead\" prefetch pattern working elsewhere in her own code, so porting it into the speech queue is the natural next step.",
